  "coding_notes": [
    "GAP-CANDIDATE set_notation — q21(a),(b),(c), 3 parts, 3 marks, each asking to LIST THE MEMBERS of a set given in notation (complement, intersection, union). This is the MEMBERSHIP form of set work, spec Foundation 1.5 — no n() anywhere on this paper or any coded Foundation paper. Tagged venn_diagrams as an INTERIM measure, and this is the one interim tag that MIS-claims rather than under-claims: venn_diagrams costs 4 and all four are probability skills, so a student who listed the members of a complement is currently recorded as understanding mutually exclusive events and combined events, having demonstrated no probability at all. Three parts here, so this candidate is at 3 of the minParts=4 bar on the Foundation slice from 8 coded papers.",
    "q4 tagged simple_arithmetic throughout: differences between negative temperatures. docs/coding-a-paper.md records directed number as CHECKED, NOT A GAP — sign handling belongs to the misconception layer, not the taxonomy.",
    "q1(b) tagged decimals (place value, house rule); q1(a),(d),(e) tagged simple_arithmetic for ordering integers and writing one in words. Same split as Jun25 2F q1.",
    "q2(a) tagged properties_of_2d_shapes, the node added 2026-09-04 that closed exactly this gap (naming a triangle and a quadrilateral).",
    "q7 tagged angles_in_polygons first: the quadrilateral angle sum carries the question, with angles on a straight line as the second step. The 'give a reason for each stage' mark is a B1 in the split.",
    "q10 tagged proportion first: a scale diagram measured and converted, then a rate. The map-scale precedent in docs/coding-a-paper.md puts the scale reading on ratio/proportion rather than on converting_measurements."
  ],
